    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are leaning heavily into the top of the order tonight, with **Yordan Alvarez** (73.06) and **Kyle Schwarber** (65.53) anchoring the lineup as the clear strongest plays. **Yordan Alvarez** remains an auto-start despite facing a tough arm in Castillo, bolstered by an elite .421 xwOBA that helps him transcend SP-matchup volatility. Simultaneously, **Kyle Schwarber** benefits from a massive park-factor boost and a favorable platoon spot against Suarez, making him an essential component of today\u2019s production floor. **Trea Turner** (64.53) also projects as an elite-tier option; while his stolen base output is slightly suppressed by the threat of a quick-working pitcher, his position at leadoff and platoon advantage make him a high-efficiency engine for the Zebras.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical challenges, most notably the high-risk deployment of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (42.58). While his elite sprint speed makes him a high-leverage asset in our SB-starved 5x5 format, he is facing a sub-3.00 xERA arm in Sale and suffering from a significant platoon disadvantage, keeping his score dangerously close to our \"below floor\" threshold. Consequently, **Dillon Dingler** (33.06) remains the most notable bench decision; he was considered for the C1 slot, but his exposure to McLean\u2014a pitcher with an elite 2.93 xERA\u2014coupled with a negative platoon split, forced the optimizer to bench him in favor of **Gary Sanchez**, who offers a more stable projection in a softer matchup. Management remains alert to the potential for defensive substitutions or late-inning fatigue, but barring weather interruptions, the Zebras look prepared to maximize efficiency across our core categories.",
